 {
  "id": "ukmt-pink-2018-23",
  "bank": "ukmt",
  "source": {
   "contest": "UKMT Pink Kangaroo",
   "paper": "2018",
   "year": 2018,
   "number": 23,
   "url": "https://ukmt.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/pink-2018-q.pdf"
  },
  "grade": "9-10",
  "points": 6,
  "blankPoints": null,
  "wrongPoints": null,
  "timeMinutes": null,
  "type": "mc",
  "prompt": "At each vertex of the 18-gon in the picture a number should be written which is equal to the sum of the numbers at the two adjacent vertices. Two of the numbers are given. What number should be written at the vertex $P$?",
  "image": "qimages/ukmt/pink-2018/q23.webp",
  "choices": [
   {
    "key": "A",
    "text": "2018"
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "text": "38"
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "text": "18"
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "text": "$-20$"
   },
   {
    "key": "E",
    "text": "$-38$"
   }
  ],
  "answer": "B",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "The numbers repeat every 6 vertices",
    "body": "Let two adjacent numbers be $a$ and $b$. The next numbers are $b-a$, then $-a$, $-b$, $a-b$, and then $a$, $b$ again. So the pattern repeats every 6 vertices. Since $18=3\\times6$ the pattern fits exactly three times round the polygon.\n\nCounting round from $P$ as vertex 0, the vertices marked 20 and 18 are vertices 7 and 11, which are in the same places in the 6-cycle as the neighbours of $P$ (vertices 1 and 17, since $7\\equiv1$ and $11\\equiv17\\pmod 6$). So the neighbours of $P$ hold 20 and 18. Since each number is the sum of its two neighbours, $P=20+18=38$.\n\n**Answer: (B) 38**"
   }
  ],
